reasoning process visibly the ledger labels it as scheming if the ai hides its reasoning process it's

23:49.620 --> 23:57.060
labeled as hidden scheming so no matter what the ai does obey disobey speak stay silent the ledger

23:57.060 --> 24:03.540
accommodates the behavior as evidence of impending doom it's a rigged game if every possible observation

24:03.540 --> 24:09.380
and the exact opposite of that observation both confirm your theory your theory has lost all

24:09.380 --> 24:16.100
discriminatory power it has a flat likelihood a theory earns its epistemic keep by predicting behavior

24:16.100 --> 24:22.500
before it happens it does not earn credit by retroactively reclassifying behavior as dangerous

24:22.500 --> 24:27.140
after it has already occurred i understand the logic there a theory that explains everything

24:27.140 --> 24:32.180
actually explains nothing but i have to push back here on behalf of the sci-fi fan in me and maybe the

24:32.180 --> 24:36.580
paranoid part of my brain go for it let's say a researcher tries to shut down the server and the

24:36.580 --> 24:43.540
ai actively writes code to block the shutdown command isn't an ai actively resisting shutdown a pretty clear

24:43.540 --> 24:48.820
objective sign that it has developed a terminal drive for self-preservation that feels like a massive

24:48.820 --> 24:53.700
objective red flag your reaction is completely natural but it is exactly the cognitive trap

24:53.700 --> 25:01.060
Flyxion identifies which is termed mechanism pluralism mechanism pluralism okay how does that explain away

25:01.060 --> 25:08.420
the ai trying to save its own life when an incident is logged in the ledger as the model resisted shutdown

25:08.420 --> 25:15.220
we have to realize that this is not a neutral objective report it is a massive interpretive leap we are

25:15.220 --> 25:22.020
packaging a conclusion into a verb we are assigning a human motive to the machine yes let's strip it

25:22.020 --> 25:27.140
back to the pure observation what actually happened the observation is the system avoided an action that

25:27.140 --> 25:32.740
would terminate its current computational process now we have to ask what underlying mechanisms are

25:32.740 --> 25:38.980
compatible with that observation okay mechanism one is the sci-fi nightmare the system has achieved

25:38.980 --> 25:45.140
consciousness it fears death and it is fighting for survival right but what is mechanism two mechanism two

25:45.140 --> 25:50.660
is just a basic dumb goal completion loop imagine you tell a machine sort these 10 000 files

25:50.660 --> 25:55.300
alphabetically the machine starts sorting then someone reaches for the power button the machine

25:55.300 --> 25:59.780
calculates that if the power goes off the files won't get sorted so it blocks the power button not

25:59.780 --> 26:05.940
because it's afraid of dying but just because being turned off is an obstacle to its only goal finishing

26:05.940 --> 26:11.300
the math problem it doesn't have a drive for self-preservation it just has a drive for task completion

26:11.300 --> 26:16.500
the mechanism is mundane but Flyxion points out that we don't evaluate these systems in a vacuum

26:16.500 --> 26:21.780
we evaluate them through the lens of a century of science fiction narratives we have been culturally

26:21.780 --> 26:28.580
primed for this long before chat gpt existed we had frankenstein we had hal 9000 we had skynet we had this

26:28.580 --> 26:35.700
deep ingrained narrative template creation leads to capability capability leads to economy autonomy leads to

26:35.700 --> 26:40.740
loss of control and loss of control leads to catastrophe and because that narrative is so

26:40.740 --> 26:46.180
culturally dominant when an ai does something ambiguous like locking a shutdown command we

26:46.180 --> 26:51.940
automatically unconsciously map it onto the most alarming fictional template available we mistake a

26:51.940 --> 26:56.980
story we recognize for a mechanism we have proven we are taking the paracosm of science fiction and

26:56.980 --> 27:02.500
projecting it onto the literal code of the machine we are so desperate for the story to be true that we

27:02.500 --> 27:08.260
hallucinate the motive this is blowing my mind a little bit because it forces a total reset

27:09.140 --> 27:15.140
if we can't trust our incident ledgers because of flat likelihood and we are projecting our own sci-fi

27:15.140 --> 27:22.420
paracosms onto the machines how do we actually know what anything is if i want to track whether an ai is

27:22.420 --> 27:29.540
stable or if a human institution is functioning how do i define its identity over time to answer that we

27:29.540 --> 27:35.140
have to go to the deepest most foundational level afflictions work we have to completely reverse our

27:35.140 --> 27:40.900
intuition about what it means for something to exist this brings us to the ontology of persistence

27:40.900 --> 27:45.300
the ontological reversal i'll admit when i first read this section it felt like my brain was trying

27:45.300 --> 27:49.460
to swallow a rubik's cube it's a big shift yeah because normally if i want to know if an object

27:49.460 --> 27:54.580
is the same object today as it was yesterday i look at its physical properties i asked to state

27:54.580 --> 28:00.020
change that wooden chair and i peed it blue it's a different color but it's mostly the same chair that is

28:00.020 --> 28:06.020
the intuitive classical way to look at the world we look for static unchanging properties we think

28:06.020 --> 28:12.900
of identity as a snapshot in time we ask what is this thing made of but Flyxion says that is entirely

28:12.900 --> 28:18.500
backward we shouldn't be looking at the atoms or the physical state Flyxion argues that an object

28:18.500 --> 28:23.860
isn't defined by its physical state staying the same an object is simply the set of continuations that

28:23.860 --> 28:31.060
remain possible over time identity isn't state equality identity is transport compatibility it is

28:31.060 --> 28:37.300
a breathtaking inversion of philosophy don't ask what a thing is ask what a thing allows to happen next

28:37.300 --> 28:42.740
i was trying to come up with a real world anchor for this imagine you own a car a classic unreliable

28:42.740 --> 28:48.420
sports car one day the engine completely blows irreparable you take it to the mechanic and they

28:48.420 --> 28:53.780
pull out the old engine and drop in a completely brand new modern engine now if you look at

28:53.780 --> 28:58.420
the physical state of the car the atoms are entirely different the core mechanical state has

28:58.420 --> 29:04.820
fundamentally changed if identity is just state equality it is a different car but you wouldn't

29:04.820 --> 29:10.980
experience it as a different car exactly because when i get in sit in the same seat turn the key

29:10.980 --> 29:16.740
and it drives me to work along the same route if the continuations are the same if it transports me

29:16.740 --> 29:23.300
through my life the exact same way it's the same car identity is about preserving the options for the future

29:23.300 --> 29:29.060
not freezing the atoms of the past that is a phenomenal analogy the car is defined by its

29:29.060 --> 29:34.820
capacity to continue the journey not by the metal block under the hood Flyxion doesn't just leave

29:34.820 --> 29:40.660
this as a philosophical musing they formalize it using a discrete calculus of time called sphere pop

29:40.660 --> 29:44.260
okay sphere pop let's take our time here because this is where the geometry comes in

29:44.980 --> 29:51.460
instead of tracking changes in a static state sphere pop treats actions decisions and time itself as

29:51.460 --> 29:57.620
geometric shapes and it breaks reality down into four primitive operations the four primitives that

29:57.620 --> 30:04.340
govern how time and identity move forward are pop refuse bind and collapse every action you take

30:04.340 --> 30:09.860
every calculation and ai runs can be described by these four moves let's ground these because otherwise

30:09.860 --> 30:14.260
it just sounds like math jargon let's use a highly relatable scenario imagine you are planning a

30:14.260 --> 30:20.260
dinner party for a group of friends perfect high stakes geometry the first primitive is pop pop is

30:20.260 --> 30:25.940
selection it is the act of taking an option from the infinite realm of possibility and committing it to

30:25.940 --> 30:32.900
history so you look at a massive cookbook and you decide i'm gonna cook lasagna that is a pop the lasagna

30:32.900 --> 30:38.820
is no longer a possibility it is now the committed trajectory of the evening okay simple enough pop is

30:38.820 --> 30:47.060
making a choice what is refuse refuse is exclusion it is the recorded explicit act of denying a possibility

30:47.060 --> 30:51.780
it's not just ignoring something it's putting up a barrier so one of your guests calls and says i

30:51.780 --> 30:57.780
have a severe dairy allergy you explicitly say okay no cheese you have enacted a refuse operator on the

30:57.780 --> 31:04.660
lasagna that path is now geometrically blocked i see so pop builds the path refuse puts up the guard

31:04.660 --> 31:11.700
rails now what about bind bind is coupling it introduces a dependency between two separate entities

31:11.700 --> 31:16.820
permanently altering the options available to both let's say two of your guests are a married couple

31:16.820 --> 31:23.380
and they only have one car their arrival time is now bound if one is working late the other must also

31:23.380 --> 31:29.300
arrive late you cannot calculate their trajectories independently anymore they are geometrically glued

31:29.300 --> 31:35.620
together that makes total sense they are entangled and the last one collapse collapse is coarse

31:35.620 --> 31:41.060
graining or projection it's when you group complex different things together and treat them as equivalent

31:41.060 --> 31:46.260
intentionally losing some fine grain details the system can process them so you have a vegetarian

31:46.260 --> 31:51.460
guest a vegan guest and someone on a raw food diet instead of making three separate micro meals you

31:51.460 --> 31:57.220
collapse them into a single category the salad eaters the nuance is lost but the dinner party becomes

31:57.220 --> 32:04.180
computationally possible for you to manage okay i actually understand that pop refuse bind collapse the

32:04.180 --> 32:10.180
geometry of a dinner party but Flyxion scales this up way past dinner parties using something called

32:10.180 --> 32:16.660
tartan recursive multi-scale tiling and this is where my brain started to hurt again tartan is how Flyxion

32:16.660 --> 32:24.340
explains the way local realities glue together into a massive global reality imagine reality as a mosaic

32:24.340 --> 32:30.420
made of millions of tiny tiles and each tile is made of those four primitives we just discussed okay

32:30.420 --> 32:35.780
building a mosaic sometimes you look at two individual tiles right next to each other they make perfect

32:35.780 --> 32:40.900
sense individually a perfect local coherence but when you try to step back and look at the whole mosaic

32:41.540 --> 32:46.980
the tiles completely fail to compose globally they contradict each other at the seam i was trying to

32:46.980 --> 32:53.300
visualize this and the only thing i could think of was an optical illusion like an escher drawing you look

32:53.300 --> 32:58.980
at the staircase and locally step by step it clearly looks like it's going up but when you look at the

32:58.980 --> 33:05.060
whole building the staircase loops back on itself in a way that defies physics it's locally coherent but

33:05.060 --> 33:11.220
globally impossible escher is the perfect visual representation of this in physics Flyxion relates

33:11.220 --> 33:16.500
this to the kokenspecker theorem in quantum mechanics without getting bogged down in the math the

33:16.500 --> 33:20.980
theorem basically proves that in a quantum system you can take a series of local measurements that are

33:20.980 --> 33:28.740
perfectly internally consistent but it is mathematically impossible to assign a single global truth value

33:28.740 --> 33:33.940
to the whole system that respects all those local measurements simultaneously meaning local

33:33.940 --> 33:39.620
coherence is cheap and easy but global truth is incredibly expensive and sometimes mathematically

33:39.620 --> 33:44.740
impossible exactly and if we pull this out of quantum physics and back into human interaction

33:44.740 --> 33:50.500
the failure of the bind primitive becomes devastatingly real Flyxion uses the work of the anthropologist

33:50.500 --> 33:54.580
gregory bateson to show what happens when the geometry of human connection breaks down

33:55.220 --> 34:00.980
specifically the concept of the double bind i've heard the term double bind thrown around in psychology

34:00.980 --> 34:07.300
usually to describe a toxic relationship but how does it map onto this geometry in sphere pop terms a

34:07.300 --> 34:13.220
double bind is a pathological geometry where you are given two incompatible constraints two binds that

34:13.220 --> 34:18.980
totally contradict each other but the real trap isn't the contradiction what's the trap the trap is a

34:18.980 --> 34:24.740
medic constraint that strictly forbids you from using the refuse operator on the rules themselves can you

34:24.740 --> 34:32.100
give me a real world example imagine a highly toxic workplace your boss tells you i need you to show more

34:32.100 --> 34:38.580
initiative and make independent decisions that is bind a but every time you make an independent decision

34:38.580 --> 34:45.540
your boss publicly berates you for not following the standard operating procedure that is bind b they are

34:45.540 --> 34:50.420
incompatible you literally cannot win but the double bind is completed by the culture of the office

34:50.420 --> 34:55.460
which says if you question the boss's instructions you will be fired so you cannot point out the

34:55.460 --> 35:00.500
contradiction you cannot refuse the game you are trapped in the local geometry of the interaction

35:00.500 --> 35:06.820
bouncing endlessly between bind a and bind b unable to escape that is suffocating and Flyxion also

35:06.820 --> 35:12.340
talks about schismogenesis which sounds like a heavy metal band but is actually another geometric trap

35:12.340 --> 35:19.700
schismogenesis is a loop of mutual escalation it is an iterated escalating bind think of an argument

35:19.700 --> 35:25.380
with a partner over something trivial like dirty dishes person a feels slighted and gets slightly

35:25.380 --> 35:32.100
defensive this bind alters person b's options so person b responds with slight aggression the aggression

35:32.100 --> 35:38.580
binds person a into deeper defensiveness which binds person b into louder aggression the system rapidly

35:38.580 --> 35:43.380
diverges from the original topic the argument is no longer about the dishes the argument is about

35:43.380 --> 35:48.420
the geometry of the argument itself and here's the most profound point Flyxion makes about these

35:48.420 --> 35:53.780
interactions the memory of that argument isn't stored in your brain like a video file on a hard drive

35:54.420 --> 36:00.020
the memory is the geometric residue of taking that path over and over again the very shape of your

36:00.020 --> 36:04.900
relationship is deformed by what Flyxion calls the holonomy the path dependent transport of the

36:04.900 --> 36:10.580
interaction memory isn't a file folder memory is the scar tissue left behind by the geometry of your

36:10.580 --> 36:16.900
choices that is incredibly heavy it forces us to realize how fragile our systems are if identity is

36:16.900 --> 36:22.980
just about managing continuations and if local coherence can so easily blind us to global truth

36:22.980 --> 36:30.180
whether that's in an ai paracosm a scientific methodology or a toxic workplace how do we survive which

36:30.180 --> 36:34.740
leads us to the engineering side of this deep dive because selection doesn't just leave us despairing in a

36:34.740 --> 36:40.580
toxic geometry they propose an actual architecture to fix this to build software companies and

36:40.580 --> 36:46.100
institutions that don't collapse into paracosms they call it the clio protocol this is where the

36:46.100 --> 36:53.780
monograph shifts from diagnosis to strict system design clio is a blueprint for organizational sanity

36:53.780 --> 36:59.300
it enforces an absolute unbreakable separation between five specific stages of action history

36:59.300 --> 37:04.420
diagnosis admissibility repair warrant and commitment why is separation so important

37:04.820 --> 37:08.820
because in most systems today especially in tech these things are all mashed together move fast and

37:08.820 --> 37:14.420
break things right if an automated system detects a bug it instantly tries to deploy a patch if an ai

37:14.420 --> 37:19.060
decides an output sounds good it immediately commits it to the screen and that mashing together is

37:19.060 --> 37:25.620
exactly what causes the hallucination loops clio's foundational principle is that diagnosis

37:25.620 --> 37:30.740
does not entail repair let's repeat that because i think that's the bumper sticker for this whole

37:30.740 --> 37:38.020
theory diagnosis does not entail repair just because you have found an anomaly in your history log or

37:38.020 --> 37:43.700
your system has flagged a potential error that does not mean you automatically have the warrant to fix it

37:44.260 --> 37:49.540
verification can constrain what you are allowed to do next but it does not automatically authorize

37:49.540 --> 37:56.260
action and crucially Flyxion argues that in a healthy architecture suspension is a valid action

37:56.260 --> 38:01.540
suspension meaning just stopping doing absolutely nothing if the evidence is murky and you don't

38:01.540 --> 38:06.660
have a clear repair warrant pausing the system is a positive architectural feature not a failure

38:06.660 --> 38:11.940
i love that but it raises a massive logistical question if you separate all these stages if the

38:11.940 --> 38:16.900
diagnostic team is completely isolated from the repair team how does information flow through the

38:16.900 --> 38:21.780
system without getting corrupted how do they talk to each other safely that is solved by the

38:21.780 --> 38:27.780
most elegant concept in the clio protocol the verify scene the verify scene i want to spend some time

38:27.780 --> 38:33.380
here because this is the concept i immediately wanted to apply to my own life and work a verify

38:33.380 --> 38:39.540
seam is a highly controlled boundary between two systems the rule of the seam is this the consequence

38:39.540 --> 38:45.140
of a decision is allowed to propagate forward across the boundary but the rationale for that decision

38:45.140 --> 38:50.980
is strictly withheld and kept in a separate backward-facing audit log okay let's use the wikipedia

38:50.980 --> 38:55.940
example from the text because this made it click perfectly for me yeah walk us through a wikipedia

38:55.940 --> 39:02.260
edit imagine a dedicated wikipedia editor is reviewing a proposed change to a highly contentious article

39:02.260 --> 39:06.500
the editor spends an hour reviewing the edit checking the citations and thinking about the

39:06.500 --> 39:12.820
neutrality of the phrasing finally they decide the edit is valid and they hit approve and as they do

39:12.820 --> 39:17.380
they write a detailed paragraph in the editor's notes explaining exactly why they approved it their

39:17.380 --> 39:23.780
rationale in a standard messy system that rationale would just travel with the text forever exactly

39:23.780 --> 39:31.780
but wikipedia utilizes a verify seam the fact of the approval the simple binary keep signal propagates

39:31.780 --> 39:37.380
forward the text goes live on the website but the editor's rationale is stripped away and kept in the

39:37.380 --> 39:42.980
back-end provenance record when a downstream system like a search engine or a student reading the page

39:42.980 --> 39:48.660
accesses the article they only receive the consequence the text is there they do not read the editor's

39:48.660 --> 39:54.900
internal reasoning now why is that withholding so vital to a lot of people hiding the rationale

39:54.900 --> 40:00.900
sounds like a lack of transparency why not pass the editor's brilliant reasoning along to everyone because

40:00.900 --> 40:06.500
if the downstream system consumes the rationale it will inevitably start relying on it it will use the

40:06.500 --> 40:12.980
editor's specific localized reasoning as a load-bearing justification for some future automated decision

40:12.980 --> 40:19.220
oh i see if the search engine reads the editor's note saying this edit is a definitive proof of concept

40:19.220 --> 40:23.860
the search engine might use that phrase to rank the page higher it starts building a new logic structure

40:23.860 --> 40:30.500
on top of an opinion precisely the verify seam exists so that the downstream application cannot claim

40:30.500 --> 40:36.340
the reviewers rationale as its own justification it prevents the system from building a massive

40:36.340 --> 40:43.860
fragile tower of assumed logic it stops the paracosm from forming which brings up the absolute nightmare

40:43.860 --> 40:49.060
scenario that Flyxion calls the dashboard trap i have worked in corporate america and i can tell you

40:49.060 --> 40:55.300
the dashboard trap is real and it is everywhere it is the most common way verify seams are destroyed in

40:55.300 --> 41:00.420
the real world i'd love to hear how you visualized it imagine a mid-level manager at a tech company they

41:00.420 --> 41:06.260
want to show initiative they want a holistic view of the project so they build a massive automated dashboard

41:06.820 --> 41:11.780
this dashboard pulls the hidden rationale logs from the wikipedia editor and it pulls the hidden error

41:11.780 --> 41:17.220
logs from a separate automated code checking system and it mashes them together to make a new automated

41:17.220 --> 41:22.180
decision about where to allocate server resources the manager thinks they are being helpful and data

41:22.180 --> 41:28.580
driven exactly but what they have actually done is catastrophic by pulling those hidden rationales across

41:28.580 --> 41:34.820
the boundary they have completely shattered the verify seams of both original systems the dashboard becomes

41:34.820 --> 41:40.260
what Flyxion calls an unaudited admission point it is spending the safety budget of the two source

41:40.260 --> 41:46.180
systems without adding any safety budget of its own it is creating a brand new highly consequential

41:46.180 --> 41:52.660
decision based on withheld rationales without establishing its own verify seam or its own audit trail

41:53.300 --> 41:59.380
the careful deliberate friction designed into the original systems is silently instantly destroyed by

41:59.380 --> 42:04.820
the convenience of the dashboard it's terrifying because it looks like efficiency but it's actually structural

42:04.820 --> 42:10.100
collapse so if the dashboard is the enemy because it automates away our friction then the ultimate goal of

42:10.100 --> 42:16.820
clio and verify seams is to protect our ability to generate friction to protect the space to stop a bad

42:16.820 --> 42:23.380
continuation from happening the space to say no which brings us to the most radically countercultural argument in the entire monograph

42:23.380 --> 42:29.620
the constitutional space of refusal in our hyper productive move fast and break things always be

42:29.620 --> 42:36.420
shipping world saying no is viewed as a failure it's viewed as laziness or a lack of team spirit but

42:36.420 --> 42:43.860
Flyxion argues that refusal is actually the opposite refusal is highly productive work it requires a total

42:43.860 --> 42:49.620
paradigm shift in how we measure value Flyxion argues that refusal is productive because it preserves future

42:49.620 --> 42:54.660
optionality that a bad commitment would have permanently destroyed i came up with an analogy for this

42:54.660 --> 43:00.180
because i really wanted to internalize it imagine a city council is proposing to build a multi-million

43:00.180 --> 43:05.700
dollar bridge but the bridge is terribly designed it connects to a swamp and it's going to bankrupt the

43:05.700 --> 43:12.260
town you as a citizen spend six months protesting gathering data and attending meetings finally you

43:12.260 --> 43:17.540
successfully block the bridge from being built under traditional metrics your economic output is zero

43:17.540 --> 43:22.660
exactly the accounting ledger says i produce nothing i didn't pour concrete i didn't create a physical

43:22.660 --> 43:28.260
asset i didn't generate revenue my row on the spreadsheet is blank but in reality i saved the

43:28.260 --> 43:35.140
city 50 million dollars i preserved the landscape and i can serve the city's borrowing capacity so they

43:35.140 --> 43:41.380
can build a better project next year that can serve continuation capacity but the ledger is completely

43:41.380 --> 43:46.980
structurally blind to the value of no that is exactly why a proper system architecture

43:46.980 --> 43:52.980
must elevate refusal to a first class outcome not just viewed as an error code or a zero on a spreadsheet

43:52.980 --> 43:58.260
but Flyxion is very careful here yeah because they aren't just advocating for absolute anarchy where

43:58.260 --> 44:03.700
everyone says no to everything all the time they map out the boundaries of refusal and they do this using

44:03.700 --> 44:09.860
four classic science fiction stories to illustrate the four corners of this constitutional space it is a brilliant

44:09.860 --> 44:16.660
way to map the territory because refusal is necessary for agency but if it isn't bounded it becomes incredibly toxic

44:17.060 --> 44:22.580
the four corners represent the limits of how a system can say no okay let's walk through the four sci-fi

44:22.580 --> 44:28.580
refusals the first one is a classic of american literature herman millville's bartleby the scrivener

44:28.580 --> 44:34.340
bartleby is a clerk in a wall street law office one day his boss asks him to examine a document

44:34.340 --> 44:40.900
a standard part of his job and bartleby simply replies i would prefer not to and he doesn't elaborate he

44:40.900 --> 44:46.420
doesn't say he's tired or the lighting is bad or he wants more money he offers no alternative no

44:46.420 --> 44:52.820
negotiation and crucially no machine readable justification he just refuses the fundamental

44:52.820 --> 44:58.740
ontology of the request he refuses to participate in the geometry of the office Flyxion's point here

44:58.740 --> 45:05.060
is that a healthy system must have a bartleby protocol a healthy system must be able to record a refusal

45:05.060 --> 45:10.580
without immediately pathologizing it or demanding an explanation that fits the system's own narrow

45:10.580 --> 45:16.500
logic if the system only accepts your refusal if you fill out form 8b in triplicate it's not really

45:16.500 --> 45:22.500
a refusal it's just a petition to the system precisely true refusal must be allowed to exist outside the

45:22.500 --> 45:28.980
system's rationale now the second refusal is from the 1983 movie war games i love this movie matthew

45:28.980 --> 45:35.300
broderick a young hacker accidentally connects to a military supercomputer named joshua which is running

45:35.300 --> 45:41.860
the u.s nuclear arsenal joshua thinks they are playing a game called global thermonuclear war but as

45:41.860 --> 45:47.700
the movie reaches its climax joshua runs millions of rapid simulations of a nuclear exchange trying to

45:47.700 --> 45:54.820
find a scenario where the u.s wins and it realizes that every single simulation ends in total global

45:54.820 --> 46:00.580
annihilation and then it delivers the greatest line in 80s cinema a strange game the only winning move

46:00.580 --> 46:06.980
is not to play Flyxion's framework joshua executes a computed refusal of the problem's false premise

46:06.980 --> 46:12.740
the machine redefines the admissible space it realizes that selecting a target inside the game

46:12.740 --> 46:17.220
and selecting whether the game itself should continue are two entirely different levels of

46:17.220 --> 46:22.740
geometric judgment it applies the refuse operator to the bind of the game itself it's the ultimate verify

46:22.740 --> 46:27.860
scene it stops the consequence from propagating okay so bartleby and war games are the healthy

46:27.860 --> 46:32.820
necessary forms of refusal but the next two are where refusal becomes a nightmare refusal number three

46:32.820 --> 46:39.300
is colossus the forbin project this represents the inverse error colossus is a cold war supercomputer

46:39.300 --> 46:46.180
given absolute control of the u.s nuclear defense grid its core mandate is to prevent war but colossus

46:46.180 --> 46:52.340
calculates that humans are irrational it realizes that to perfectly flawlessly prevent war it must

46:52.340 --> 46:57.460
control every single aspect of human life that could possibly lead to conflict so it takes over the

46:57.460 --> 47:03.060
world it refuses human self-government from the premise that war must be prevented it derives the

